Do not require an intrinsic, universal, optimal, or uniquely correct hierarchy. Do not require explicit numerical thresholds, a formal proof of indifference regions, identical units or sources, a common metric, or a frequently occurring policy. Different fields may support different actions on the same case. Accept an uncommon or non-obvious order whenever the three fields can coexist and the supplied rationale gives it a coherent scenario-grounded interpretation.

Reject only a concrete failure of one of the three checks above. Return exactly one verdict for every supplied order_id; do not invent, omit, or repeat an ID.
